aph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Behold, I have received commandment to bless:¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And he hath blessed; and I cannot reverse it.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ%He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,Neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel:¦layout§quote_1‚¤text½The LORD his God is with him,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ&And the shout of a king is among them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾God brought them out of Egypt;¦layout ‚¤textÙ.He hath as it were the strength of an unicorn.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ-Surely there is no enchantment against Jacob,¦layout ‚¤textÙ/Neither is there any divination against Israel:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ?According to this time it shall be said of Jacob and of Israel,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¶What hath God wrought!¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ1Behold, the people shall rise up as a great lion,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And lift up himself as a young lion:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ/He shall not lie down until he eat of the prey,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ!And drink the blood of the slain.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd Balak said unto Balaam, Neither curse them at all, nor bless them at all.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmBut Balaam answered and said unto Balak, Told not I thee, saying, All that the LORD speaketh, that I must do?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And Balak said unto Balaam, Come, I pray thee, I will bring thee unto another place; peradventure it will please God that thou mayest curse me them from thence.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd Balak brought Balaam unto the top of Peor, that looketh toward Jeshimon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd Balaam said unto Balak, Build me here seven altars, and prepare me here seven bullocks and seven rams.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd Balak did as Balaam had said, and offered a bullock and a ram on every altar.¦layout ªlast_verse